{
  "_id": "tg-rod",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Jacob took him rods, Gen. 30:37. Moses took the rod of God in his hand, Ex. 4:20. Aaron cast down his rod before Pharaoh, Ex. 7:10. whatsoever passeth under the rod, the tenth shall be holy, Lev. 27:32. take of every one of them a rod, Num. 17:2. rod of Aaron for the house of Levi was budded, Num. 17:8 (Heb. 9:4). Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron, Ps. 2:9. thy rod and thy staff they comfort me, Ps. 23:4. Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, Ps. 89:32. Lord shall send the rod of thy strength out of Zion, Ps. 110:2. He that spareth his rod hateth his son, Prov. 13:24. rod of correction shall drive it far from him, Prov. 22:15. rod for the fool’s back, Prov. 26:3. rod and reproof give wisdom, Prov. 29:15. rod of his oppressor, as in the day of Midian, Isa. 9:4 (2 Ne. 19:4). his rod was upon the sea, Isa. 10:26 (2 Ne. 20:26). come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, Isa. 11:1 (2 Ne. 21:1; D&C 113:3). smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, Isa. 11:4 (2 Ne. 21:4; 30:9). I will cause you to pass under the rod, Ezek. 20:37.",
